WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.435
-Eddie, part of being a legend
means that you spend some time

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:06.072
with other legends, and I was
thinking that I could say

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:09.042
maybe the name of another iconic
person and you can tell me

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.844
the first memory or story
that comes to your mind.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.046
Is that okay?

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.981
-Yeah, sure, yeah.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:18.017
I don't know how many legends
I've met.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.486
-I have 104 listed here.

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:23.189
-You have 104 actual legends?

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.126
-No, no, no, I only have
like five legends.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.562
Alright. Here we go.
Richard Pryor.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.833
-He was so nice and sweet to me,
and I loved to make him laugh.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.904
There was nothing more rewarding
than to say something

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.206
and have Richard Pryor --
[ Laughs as Pryor ]

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:45.879
That's how he laughed.
[ Laughs as Pryor ]

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.149
When Richard did that,
you would be like...

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.684
To make Richard laugh? Yeah.
-Right?

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:55.454
-He was so, so, so sweet to me.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.323
-How about Rodney Dangerfield?

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.492
-Rodney Dangerfield --
I met him when I was young.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.727
He gave me, like, bad advice.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.663
I met him when I was like 17.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.799
I was 17. I played the Comic
Strip down in Fort Lauderdale,

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.769
and Rodney Dangerfield came in
and bumped everybody.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.004
It was like,
"Dangerfield's going up."

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.204
And all the comics are like,
"Dangerfield!"

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:13.373
He went up and did...

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.874
[ As Dangerfield ]
Yeah, no, I tell you --

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.576
[ Normal voice ]
And all that stuff he was doing.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.977
And I was like,
"Mr. Dangerfield, please,"

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.278
after he came off and he killed.

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:20.679
I said, "Please watch my show."

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:22.048
I wanted to go up after him,
right,

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.415
'cause I thought
I was a hot shot.

00:01:23.415 --> 00:01:25.118
I went up there
and I crushed it.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.852
And I came off
and Dangerfield's like...

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.821
[ As Dangerfield ]
Yeah, you know, you use a lot of

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.889
foul language
and you say [bleep].

00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:32.258
You use that language.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.726
Where are you gonna go
talking that kind of stuff?

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.327
[ Normal voice ]
He gave me all this stuff.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:37.596
Like, all the wind
came out of my sails.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:39.299
I was like, "Ugh, Dangerfield."

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.367
Then, you know,
three years went by.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:45.238
I get on "Saturday Night Live,"
and three years go by.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:49.475
I'm at Caesar's Palace in
Las Vegas, and I'm at a urinal.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.944
And Dangerfield walks in,

00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:54.080
and he comes in the urinal
right next to me.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.115
And I look over and he looks
over at me and says...

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.216
[ As Dangerfield ]
"Hey, who knew?"

00:01:57.216 --> 00:02:00.085
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:01.854
[ Normal voice ] That's
my Rodney Dangerfield story.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.056
-At least he was funny.
-He was totally real with it.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.658
He was totally funny with it.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.926
-[ As Dangerfield ]
Hey, who knew, huh?

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.094
-[ As Dangerfield ]
Hey, who knew?

00:02:09.094 --> 00:02:11.564
-[ Normal voice ] My favorite
Rodney joke, he goes,

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.933
"My wife's cooking is so bad.
Are you kidding me?

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.602
I mean, since when does
toast have bones?"

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.204
-[ as Dangerfield ] You know?

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.273
Since when does toast
have bones, you know?

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.942
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.576
-Oh, my gosh.
-I went to my dentist.

00:02:24.576 --> 00:02:25.879
He told me my teeth are yellow.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.412
He told me wear a brown necktie.

00:02:27.412 --> 00:02:30.083
You know what I mean?

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.051
[ Normal voice ]
So to have that guy tell you,

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.919
"I don't think
you have a future, kid,"

00:02:33.919 --> 00:02:35.455
I was like, "What the [bleep]?"

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:38.190
-Heartbreaking.
-I was crestfallen.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:39.459
But he kept it real.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.826
-"Hey, who knew?"
is unbelievable.

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:42.095
That's perfect.
-"Hey, who knew?"

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:46.732
It was like the perfectly timed
three-year gap.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:49.102
Three-year buildup
to that moment.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.103
And right, you look over,
he's right there.

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:53.840
"Hey, who knew?" Perfect.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.441
-Good line.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.743
Muhammad Ali.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:59.978
-Oh, Muhammad Ali is my hero.

00:02:59.978 --> 00:03:03.115
That's my hero.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:07.053
-I remember you --
You did Ali, didn't you?

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.188
-Yeah, I've done impressions
of him,

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:13.258
but there's not another person
that inspired me

00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:15.794
more in life than Muhammad Ali.

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:21.600
I think he's the greatest
African-American

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.002
that ever lived,
that ever walked the Earth.

00:03:24.002 --> 00:03:29.175
Like, no one had the impact
like Muhammad Ali.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.444
-And you got to hang out
with him?

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.079
-Oh, I didn't get to hang out
with him.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.147
I met him a couple of times.
-Oh.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:36.649
-I met him a few times.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.651
And he gave me
a really cool thing.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:42.121
For my 40th birthday, he gave me
a plaque with a glove on it.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.223
It was like, "From your brother
Muhammad Ali."

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:47.627
My most treasured thing is this
cool little plaque from Ali.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.729
-Gosh.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.465
Do you remember
that Ed Bradley interview he did

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:55.133
on "60 Minutes,"
him and Ed Bradley?

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.969
It was later, as he --

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.071
-Oh, after, yeah, when he
pretended he was sleeping?

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.206
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.708
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.209
And then he acted like
he was having fits.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:07.246
Yeah, it was very funny.
-He's, like, punching.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.915
-And that's one of the things
that was beautiful about Ali,

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:11.517
that he always had --

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:15.287
he was always Ali, even when
his health started to fail.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:18.090
He was never --
That spirit was still there.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.726
He was always Ali.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.193
-That's so cool.

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:25.163
-I love Muhammad Ali so much.

00:04:25.163 --> 00:04:27.132
-Well, Stevie Wonder.

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:29.101
You must have met Stevie Wonder.
You sang with him.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:31.103
-Yeah, I met Stevie.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:35.975
Yeah, Stevie's an old friend,
and I love Steve.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.543
And he's a true genius.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:40.379
Stevie's the genius --
You know how you hear people say

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.681
somebody's a genius
or this person's a genius?

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.917
Stevie Wonder is a real genius.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:49.188
If you're around him, it's like,
okay, that's what a genius is.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.958
It's like, okay,
I never seen one before.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:55.361
And when you see him,
especially if you're around him

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:58.631
and he's doing something with
music, then it's --

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.199
then you're really blown away
by it.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.367
But it don't even have to
be that.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:05.237
Just be around him
and he's just a genius.

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:08.875
-Yeah, it's almost insane
when you get to really see,

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.710
like, someone like that
and you're just like --

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.444
You go, "Yeah," and notes
just start playing like...

00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:16.048
[ Vocalizing ]

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:20.019
-Yeah, I think of all the
artists I've met ever in life,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.188
the two that I've met felt,
like, you know,

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:25.791
this otherworldly amount of
talent and genius

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:29.161
was Stevie and Prince.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:32.898
They were like,
okay, this is a genius.

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:34.600
-Yeah, and Prince --

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.537
We talked a little bit about
Prince last time you were here.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:40.105
And he was on our show
a bunch of times.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:41.874
I always tell people
if they ask me about him

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.342
that he was actually funny.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:44.743
He loved to laugh.

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:46.846
-Yeah, yeah, sense of humor,
yeah.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:50.049
Oh, another genius is McCartney.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.650
-Yeah. Of course.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.553
-I've been around --
Yeah, those three.

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.856
You know, those three.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.858
Prince, McCartney, and Stevie.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:03.162
I was like, "I'm in the presence
of a genius."

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:06.565
-Did the story
that your brother Charlie --

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:10.469
which, again, I'm sorry
to hear about his passing --

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:12.505
the story about Prince
challenging you

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:16.676
to a game of pickup basketball
that he told on "Chappelle,"

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:19.011
I'm sure that really happened,
but --

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:21.413
-That is totally
and absolutely accurate.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:23.982
-But he gave you outfits?

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:28.020
-No, we had on stuff
from the club, you know.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:32.191
So we had on club clothes,
and Prince had on that outfit

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.760
that was in the "Kiss" video

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.895
where he had the little,
like, short shirt

00:06:36.895 --> 00:06:39.197
and the leather jacket
with the buttons and stuff.

00:06:39.197 --> 00:06:40.299
He had that outfit on

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.568
and a little gold chain
around his waist.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.637
A waistlet, I think.
He had on a waistlet.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:46.438
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.438 --> 00:06:48.373
And he was like, "Yo, want to
play some basketball?"

00:06:48.373 --> 00:06:49.508
We was like, "What the [bleep]?

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:52.644
You want to play
some basketball?"

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.313
It was like,
"Alright, let's play."

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:56.481
My brother was --
It was Prince and some dude,

00:06:56.481 --> 00:06:58.217
a dude named Micki Free
that used to hang out.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.686
They used to all kind of wear
their kind of Prince clothes.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:01.887
So my brother was like,

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:04.824
"Alright, it's gonna be
shirts against blouses."

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:08.394
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.528
-And who won?

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:11.964
-And they teamed up
and the blouses won.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.133
They beat the [bleep] out of us.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:15.534
But you know what I think?

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:18.504
We had one dude on our squad
that could play named Larry,

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.540
and he didn't have no shoes,
so Prince said --

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.642
gave him some sneakers, right?

00:07:23.642 --> 00:07:26.512
And Prince wore, like,
maybe two, three sizes

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:29.281
smaller than Larry,
but Larry was so excited

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:33.418
to have Prince's sneakers on,
he put them tiny sneakers

00:07:33.418 --> 00:07:35.654
on his feet,
so he couldn't do his game.

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:37.123
-Toes all crammed up.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:38.324
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.893
-Yeah, so he couldn't execute.
So we lost.

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:42.328
The one dude that could play,

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:46.198
Prince's shoes had him shut
down, so he couldn't execute.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:47.766
-That's genius!

00:07:47.766 --> 00:07:50.269
That's the genius move.

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.304
Eddie, I always love
talking to you.

00:07:52.304 --> 00:07:54.873
I'm so happy.
Congrats on everything.

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.676
Congrats on "Coming 2 America."

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:58.811
I can't wait for the world
to see it.

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:00.779
It's gonna stream on
Amazon Prime Video

00:08:00.779 --> 00:08:01.981
beginning next Friday.

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:03.682
Thanks again for coming by.
Come whenever.

00:08:03.682 --> 00:08:05.016
-Yeah, man, I'm gonna come by.

00:08:05.016 --> 00:08:07.853
I can't wait to come by
when it's all safe to come.

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:09.688
-Yep. Oh, you're always welcome.
-Yeah, man.

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:10.857
-Thank you so much. Congrats.

